      * Gets the class name minus the package name from a {@link Class}.
      *
      * <p>
-     * This method simply gets the name using {@code Class.getName()} and then calls {@link #getShortClassName(String)}. See
-     * relevant notes there.
+     * Unlike {@link #getShortClassName(String)}, this method uses Class reflection metadata to correctly distinguish
+     * between package separators, outer classes, and inner classes. This avoids misinterpreting {@code $} characters
+     * that are part of legitimate Java identifiers (e.g., in top-level classes or nested classes whose names contain {@code $}).
+     * </p>
+     *
+     * <p>
+     * For local and anonymous classes, which have compiler-generated names, the method falls back to string-based parsing
+     * to preserve existing behavior for those special cases.
